1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,200
In every classroom, students learn at different speeds.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,200
Sometimes, a student struggles with a new concept not because they cannot learn it,

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,800
but because an earlier foundation is missing.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Teachers need to find that gap before it grows.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Meet KakshaSignal, a teacher-led adaptive learning system

6
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:30,200
built to make learning gaps visible, recommend the next best learning step,

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,500
and keep teachers in control.

8
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Sneha is struggling with Class 8 Rational Numbers.

9
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:49,500
Instead of simply marking her answer wrong,

10
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:54,000
KakshaSignal traces the stored prerequisite relationships

11
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:58,500
to identify an earlier concept that needs attention: Class 6 Fractions.

12
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:13,200
Students then follow a structured Learn, Solve, Test cycle.

13
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:18,500
They study the concept, practise with immediate feedback,

14
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:22,500
and complete an assessment.

15
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:27,500
Where supported, a parallel reassessment checks progress with different questions.

16
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:33,300
The resulting score updates the recorded mastery state and informs the next step.

17
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,000
KakshaSignal does not replace the teacher.

18
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:55,500
It gives educators explainable evidence, an overview of classroom needs,

19
00:01:55,800 --> 00:02:01,000
and control to assign, verify, or reset a learning intervention.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,200
Built with Indian classroom constraints in mind,

21
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:21,500
KakshaSignal offers selected Hindi interface translations,

22
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:26,000
reduced visual effects in low-bandwidth mode, and static-shell caching.

23
00:02:26,200 --> 00:02:31,000
Assessment and grading still require an active backend connection.

24
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:38,500
Under the interface, a deterministic prerequisite graph makes every recommendation inspectable across Classes 6 to 8.

25
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:48,000
The latest updates add signed sessions, classroom access checks, and 144 passing verification tests.

26
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:53,800
KakshaSignal helps teachers identify the gap, adapt the next step,

27
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,800
and keep every learner moving forward.
